From dc1889c8a9d52393a8211fb55180e5abbf310e29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xiangyz <xiangyz@umich.edu>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:26:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] R1 ablations: fixed_horizon (V1) and fixed_speed (V2) on
 the Study 1 protocol

Reviewer 1 asked to separate the adaptive gaze lookahead from the pace law.
Two new mpcc variants complete the 2x2 with the full model and the baseline:

- fixed_horizon: constant corridor lead fixed (not fitted) at the
  participant's mean human gaze lead at fixation onset
  (eval/eval-anchor-drive/human_gaze_horizon_10p.json), no v*T_min floor,
  free space looks at the target; pace law, replanning, T0 scan unchanged.
- fixed_speed: budget lookahead kept; corridor deadline = lead / v_type with
  one constant target speed per steering task type (the baseline's
  per-type reference-velocity parameterisation, no curvature term), fitted
  jointly, initialised at the training mean speed per type.

Simulator switches are gated (fixed_lead_speed_floor, fixed_lead_free_space,
catchup_mode target_speed, target_speed_by_type); defaults reproduce the
paper personas bit-identically. Steering task configs carry task_type.
Also carries the model_gaze_lead GAM-path fix from 8385105 so the
ablations' gaze-lead events step runs. Based on 22c349c so the fit protocol
matches the paper's Study 1 runs. See docs/r1_ablation.md.

